Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Exit Capsule Agent project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- Added dependency to package.json
- Generated package-lock.json for npm dependency management

### 2. Analytics Configuration
Modified: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Imported the Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the root layout's body element
- Placed after existing components (children and Toaster) as per best practices

## Implementation Details

This project uses:
- Next.js 16.4.2 with App Router
- TypeScript
- React 19.0.0

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the App Router pattern by:
1. Adding the Analytics import at the top of the root layout file
2. Including the `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag

The Analytics component is now configured to:
- Track page views automatically
- Send analytics data to Vercel's platform when deployed
- Work seamlessly with Next.js App Router navigation

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ TypeScript compilation passed
✅ No new linting errors introduced (existing linter warnings in carousel.tsx and use-mobile.ts are pre-existing)
✅ Analytics component properly integrated following Next.js App Router conventions

## Next Steps

To enable analytics on Vercel:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the project's Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click "Enable" in the header
4. Analytics data will start appearing after deployment and user visits

The implementation is complete and ready for deployment.
